I'll read the design review brief first, then the full design bundle, and rule only through the interaction/motion lens.{"lens":"Interaction and motion design","verdict":"changes_requested","summary":"Make TABLE↔STRATA the only layout argument, cut decorative 3D modes and free trackball, demote stagger to opt-in, and add search plus law/hazard filters so 68 tiles are findable as a reference instrument.","tension_rulings":[{"tension":1,"ruling":"cut","why":"SPHERE/HELIX/GRID add mode cost and train users that layout changes are spectacle, diluting the only motion that argues groups⊥strata."},{"tension":4,"ruling":"change","why":"Free trackball leaves tile text non-parallel and unreadably occluded; replace with constrained orthographic or face-locked views, not free 3D."}],"findings":[{"id":"F1","severity":"high","section":"Part 2 Proposed technical direction — five layouts; Part 3 tension 1","problem":"Equal-class layout switcher among TABLE, STRATA, SPHERE, HELIX, GRID makes the primary argument compete with non-semantic demos, so repeated users learn motion as chrome rather than structure.","instruction":"Ship only TABLE and STRATA as layout modes. Cut SPHERE/HELIX/GRID. If a third mode is needed later, it must assert a data axis (status, asynchrony, group, stratum, law-count, or hazard-membership)—never a decorative packing.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F2","severity":"high","section":"Part 2 trackball camera; Part 3 tension 4","problem":"A free trackball on CSS3D text tiles forces readers to fight orientation to read labels—fatal for a reference instrument used while thinking about mechanisms.","instruction":"Remove free trackball. Use a fixed orthographic (or lightly perspective) view with tiles always face-on; allow at most discrete yaw presets or a 2D pan/zoom. Prefer CSS 2D positioning with depth as sort order if face-lock is costly.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F3","severity":"high","section":"Part 2 transitions: exponential in-out + per-tile stagger","problem":"~1.5s staggered ease is a first-visit explainer; on the tenth switch it delays comparison and blocks rapid TABLE↔STRATA use.","instruction":"Default transitions ≤300ms, no stagger (or opacity-only). Offer one explicit “Show structure” / first-visit choreography with stagger. Honor reduced-motion with instant remaps and no camera paths.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F4","severity":"high","section":"Part 2 Why + atlas-layouts transitions; interrogation on orthogonality","problem":"Calling TABLE↔STRATA primary is correct, but motion alone does not make orthogonality legible if tiles only tween to new slots without preserving dual coordinates.","instruction":"During and after transition: keep stable tile identity; show continuous paths from group-column to stratum-band; persist both group and stratum labels on every tile; optionally ghost the other axis (column guides in STRATA, band guides in TABLE). Argument = remapping + dual encoding, not ease curves.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F5","severity":"medium","section":"Part 2 atlas-interaction (search listed but unspecified); 68 elements","problem":"Spatial browse of ~68 tiles across ragged columns in 3D is high cost for “open one element by symbol/name”—the dominant reference task.","instruction":"Make search the primary find path: typeahead on symbol/name/id, Enter focuses and selects, camera/layout jumps without multi-second motion. Add filters for group, stratum, status, asynchrony. Provide a flat A–Z or by-group list mode as non-spatial fallback.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F6","severity":"medium","section":"Part 1 data (29 laws, 19 hazards, bonds); Part 2 capabilities omit query UX","problem":"Laws, hazards, and bond requirements are first-class data but have no stated interaction; users cannot ask “who is in this hazard?” or “what satisfies this law?” without leaving the viz.","instruction":"Add one first-class interaction: select a law or hazard rule → highlight/filter member and non-member elements; on element select, list applicable laws, hazard membership, and bond requirements. That is the missing interaction the data demands.","basis":"principle"}],"what_to_keep":"TABLE↔STRATA as the sole primary dual-layout that can make group/stratum orthogonality visible through identity-preserving remapping—not the decorative three.js demos.","dissent_note":"Visual/delight lenses may keep SPHERE; accessibility may ban 3D entirely. Motion lens: cut demos, constrain camera."}
